> I managed to finish another game in just 2 days of
> not so intensive play - this time with orcish chaotic ranger. I have a
> question regarding vampire special attack - i encountered a lot of
> vampires this time, and they managed to downlevel me several times. I
> noticed, that after i regained level my total HP was always lower than
> before. Is it a rule, or just coincidence?

Coincidence. When you level back up, your maxHP increase is rolled
anew, just as if you had been gaining that level for the first time.
(As opposed to games like Angband and Crawl where your HP and MP are
calculated from your stats, with no random factors.)

> Also - is it possible to be very very fast in Nethack? What happens to
> Valkyrie, if she manages eat to quantum mechanics being level 6
> monster? She will be upgraded to very very fast gaining level 7? Or
> she will just stay as fast, as before?

Yes, you can be very fast, but only with speed boots (or haste self/
potion of speed). Intrinsic speed only has one binary state, present
or absent. Gaining intrinsic speed from experience level is no
different from eating a Q-mech or zapping yourself with a wand.

